            <ArticleTitle>Angiographic visualization of a right gastroepiploic artery-left circumflex coronary artery graft.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>121-4</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A 41-year-old man who underwent coronary artery bypass grafting using a gastroepiploic artery graft to the left circumflex coronary artery is reported. Subselective angiography of the right gastroepiploic artery using a steerable guidewire and coaxial catheter system is described.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
